077 planting is see-through, sim side · Keel (Opus 5.5) · 2026-10-30
Status: the rule is in and tested. The narrowed digest is in, behind a site option that the 077 adoption turns on once. The probe has been run.
Nothing is adopted or regenerated, and nothing is re-recorded. sim/data is byte-identical: a rebuild with the committed options === handover.site.json.

1. The rule (rulebook terms; tools/sim/solids.ts head, "render-only")
- needs: a kit piece placed in the Handover window, plus its kit.collide.json entry.
- changes:
  - An entry that declares `volumes: []` is render-only. It is drawn, but stands no solid: no walk cell, no sight occluder, no cover.
    The grid's digest never names it. Its stonework is a separate piece, or separate volumes, with its own entry.
  - No entry at all is NOT render-only. It is listed `unmeasured`. A civic mass still stands as its prism, as before (until now that was silent).
    buildSite refuses to build: "kit.collide.json has no entry for X, placed in the Handover window: measure it (bun run collide) or declare it render-only (volumes [])".
  - An entry with no volumes list at all is an error, read by drawnSolids before anything is placed.
  - Render-only is never inferred, from a name, a class or a height.
- who sees: nobody. A render-only piece is invisible to sight and to the walk. Planting never hides anybody (Sky 2026-10-30, "yeah, see through").
- digest (grid.collide): solidDigest covers the same fields as before (schema, frame, rule, and each piece's bounds and volumes).
  - It covers only the pieces that stand at least one solid in the window, plus the camera pole (CCTVPole). A render-only piece adds nothing.
  - A piece whose volumes all fall outside the window, or inside a building's own walls, adds nothing.
  - A volume or bounds change, or a solid piece coming or going, still moves it.
  - Why it's behind an option: today's digest names 5 placed render-only inlays (InlayBand_12_2, InlayBand_06_2, InlayArc_R4_W06/R9_W12/R2_W06).
    Turning it on therefore moves grid.collide once, and with it every recording's inputs. That should happen at the adoption's regeneration, not before.
  - The option: SiteOptions.solidDigest. `bun run sim:site --solid-digest` writes grid.collide = solidSha and grid.drawn.digest = "solid".
    optionsOfSite reads it back from the committed site, so a plain `bun run sim:site` keeps it from then on. Off (the default today), the bytes are unchanged.
  - The C# engine doesn't read grid.collide or grid.drawn's keys (Site.cs grid.Only lists "drawn"; Grid.cs never opens it), so no engine change is needed.

